Example 1.3 (Poisson Distribution) The Poisson Distribution 1.4 (with rate parameter \lambda &gt; 0) is a probability distribution on \mathcal{X} = \{0,1,2, \dots \} with probability mass function 
p(x) = \frac{ e^{-\lambda} \lambda^x }{ x! } .
 In shorthand this is denoted \mathrm{Pois}(\lambda).


